{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> Moses answered: I do two things. The first, that the people come to me to inquire of Elohim — the meaning is to inquire of His Torah. And the second, that they have a matter coming to me. And he answered the latter first: and I judge between a man and his fellow, and I make known the statutes of Elohim to the inquirer."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:36.309477321Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}